<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">
    <!-- Haven round 7, launcher icon ONLY (the user's "Fold into
         7" redesign). REPLACES round 6's white line-art house on
         a green field — no green field, no white line art
         remains anywhere in this construction.
         CONSTRUCTION (user's reference image, 2026-11-03): a
         house built from gradient segments on a cream field
         (see ic_launcher_background.xml), colorful and bright,
         not line art. The gradient runs light lime through deep
         green across the facets, with a yellow-orange center
         panel, an arched door segment on the LEFT, and a small
         yellow 4-point sparkle at the upper right.
         FACETS (same 30..78 x 30..76 envelope as round 6, so
         the safe-zone discipline carries over unchanged):
         - Roof left: apex (54,30), eave (30,52), ridge foot
           (54,52); gradient deep leaf #3E6B2F at the eave to
           light lime #9BF67C at the ridge.
         - Roof right: apex (54,30), eave (78,52), ridge foot
           (54,52); gradient light lime at the ridge to deep
           leaf at the eave.
         - Body left (36..50, 52..76): horizontal gradient
           deep leaf at the outer edge to mid green #66BB6A
           at the center.
         - Center panel (50..62, 52..76): vertical gradient
           yellow #FFD54F at the top to orange #FF8F00 at the
           bottom — the warm center.
         - Body right (62..72, 52..76): horizontal gradient
           mid green at the center to deep leaf at the outer
           edge.
         - Door (39..47, arch apex ~61, base 76): cream
           #FAF7F0, the field color — it reads as a doorway
           against every body facet, and stays cream (not
           blackened) if the background layer blackens, because
           the foreground survives intact (round 6's finding).
         - Sparkle: yellow #FFD54F 4-point star centered
           (71,37), half-size 6, clear of the roof edge
           (roof edge at y=37 is x~61.6; sparkle starts x=65).
         GRADIENT DIRECTION (deliberate): the silhouette's
         OUTER edges are deep green, the interior grades
         toward lime/yellow — so the house boundary on the
         cream field is crisp everywhere (deep leaf on cream
         is ~6:1), while the light-lime facet never has to
         carry an outer edge against cream (light lime on
         cream would be ~1.3:1, a soft edge). The light facet
         is an interior highlight, bounded by darker facets.
         SAFE ZONE (center 54,54, radius 33 — the adaptive
         66dp safe zone): roof eaves ~24.1dp out, apex 24dp,
         body corners ~28.4dp, sparkle extremes ~28.6dp — all
         outermost ink stays under ~30.7dp, so circle,
         squircle, square, rectangle, and expressive masks
         (including Samsung's default shape) never clip
         critical content. Roof overhangs the body eaves line
         by 6dp per side, as a real roofline should.
         RECENTS (the stated acceptance case): if a device
         path blackens the cream background layer, the bright
         foreground survives — lime facets, yellow-orange
         center, yellow sparkle, and cream doorway all read on
         black, and the deep-green facets are bounded by bright
         neighbors. This inverts round 5's failure (dark mark
         on blackened field) instead of repeating it.
         Vectors use real linear gradients (minSdk 26, so
         VectorDrawable gradients, API 24+, are safe); the
         legacy mipmap PNGs render the same facets, with the
         roof diagonals approximated as horizontal gradients
         (see make-legacy-icon-round7.py). -->
    <path android:pathData="M54,30 L30,52 L54,52 Z">
        <gradient
            android:type="linear"
            android:startX="30"
            android:startY="52"
            android:endX="54"
            android:endY="30"
            android:startColor="#3E6B2F"
            android:endColor="#9BF67C" />
    </path>
    <path android:pathData="M54,30 L78,52 L54,52 Z">
        <gradient
            android:type="linear"
            android:startX="54"
            android:startY="30"
            android:endX="78"
            android:endY="52"
            android:startColor="#9BF67C"
            android:endColor="#3E6B2F" />
    </path>
    <path android:pathData="M36,52 H50 V76 H36 Z">
        <gradient
            android:type="linear"
            android:startX="36"
            android:startY="64"
            android:endX="50"
            android:endY="64"
            android:startColor="#3E6B2F"
            android:endColor="#66BB6A" />
    </path>
    <path android:pathData="M50,52 H62 V76 H50 Z">
        <gradient
            android:type="linear"
            android:startX="50"
            android:startY="52"
            android:endX="50"
            android:endY="76"
            android:startColor="#FFD54F"
            android:endColor="#FF8F00" />
    </path>
    <path android:pathData="M62,52 H72 V76 H62 Z">
        <gradient
            android:type="linear"
            android:startX="62"
            android:startY="64"
            android:endX="72"
            android:endY="64"
            android:startColor="#66BB6A"
            android:endColor="#3E6B2F" />
    </path>
    <path
        android:fillColor="#FAF7F0"
        android:pathData="M39,76 V65 Q43,57 47,65 V76 Z" />
    <path
        android:fillColor="#FFD54F"
        android:pathData="M71,31 L73,35 L77,37 L73,39 L71,43 L69,39 L65,37 L69,35 Z" />
</vector>
